course: dictionary
lesson: 6950
title: One word, many meanings: pair
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pair is two things of the same kind that go together, like a pair of socks or a pair of scissors. Pair can also be a verb: to pair up means to make groups of two. «Pair the numbers from both ends to add fast: 1 + 4 = 5 and 2 + 3 = 5.» Here pair means to match two numbers together.
explain: Look at the words around pair to find its meaning. «In class we work in pairs» means two people working together. «A pair of pistols» means two pistols that go together, so the word pair tells you how many. Check by swapping in two: a pair of socks means two socks.
explain: Pair works the same way when you read a sentence about people or animals. Two friends can be a pair, and a pair of birds is two birds together. When you see pair, ask yourself: are there two things here, and do they go together?
fact: A pair is two things of the same kind that go together.
fact: «13 children make 6 pairs, and 1 child is left alone, because 6 + 6 = 12 and 12 + 1 = 13.»
fact: «N pairs» means N × 2 things, so 6 pairs is 12 things.
fact: To pair up means to make groups of two, and «in pairs» means two by two.
fact: «Tu es» and «il est» sound exactly the same, but the spelling is different: tu takes es, and il takes est.
exercise: «Mum bought a pair of socks for me.» How many socks are in one pair? | Three | *Two | One | Four
exercise: «13 children make 6 pairs, and 1 child is left alone.» How many children are in 6 pairs? | 6 | *12 | 13 | 1
exercise: Ella and Sam pair up for the quiz. What does pair up mean here? | Sing a song together | Run away fast | *Make a group of two | Count to ten
test: «Pair the numbers from both ends to add fast: 1 + 4 = 5 and 2 + 3 = 5.» Which pair of numbers makes 10? | 1 and 2 | 2 and 3 | 4 and 5 | *3 and 7
test: «At dusk the Rat dresses everybody for the expedition: ... a pair of pistols ...» How many pistols is a pair of pistols? | Four | Three | *Two | One
exam: «Small birds such as sparrows hop and leave pairs of prints, pigeons and crows walk and leave one print after another.» Which birds leave pairs of prints? | Pigeons | Frogs | *Sparrows | Crows
